<!--
    A call argument narrowed before its callee's prototype was known panicked
    non-zero mask analysis with a shift overflow.

    `f` calls through `p->fn`, whose type gives the call one 8-byte parameter
    only after type recovery has started.  By then subvariable flow has
    replaced the 8-byte RDI the call read with the 2-byte sum it holds, while
    the call's trial for RDI still says 8 bytes.  Forcing the prototype reused
    the 2-byte Varnode for the 8-byte parameter through SUBPIECE(sum:2, 0):8,
    RuleSubNormal folded the shift below it into SUBPIECE(v1, -6), and
    getNZMaskLocal shifted by 8 * -6.

    Stage / sub-stage: P4 late prototype restriction
    (`FuncCallSpecs::transfer_locked_input`), reached from
    `ActionDeindirect`.  A strict correctness fix: no option, one pass.  An
    input narrower than its parameter fails the restriction, so the function
    restarts with the call's inputs locked and the argument stays 8 bytes.

    Source (GNU as, the .text bytes verbatim below):

        f:  mov %rdi,%rcx
            xor %edx,%edx
            movzwl (%rsi),%eax
            test $0xfff,%ax
            setne %dl
            shr $0xc,%ax
            lea (%rax,%rdx,1),%rdi
            and $0x1f,%edi
            sub $8,%rsp
            call *(%rcx)
            add $8,%rsp
            ret

    #1 proves f decompiles and the argument is the zero-extended sum; #2
    proves the call goes through the typed field.
-->
